In article <5crmu5$j2v@news.corpcomm.net>, jthvedt@brookings.net (Joseph Thvedt) writes:
> I have an AS2100 running DU 3.2c and Oracle.  It has two EISA swxcr
> 3-channel disk controllers, each with a variety of RZ28s and RZ29s in
> RAID 1, 0+1, and 5.  I've been monitoring the i/o with iostat.
> 
> Does anyone have a formula, rule-of-thumb, or wild guess for the
> maximum i/o I can expect from these disks?  I think one of the RAID
> sets may be a bottleneck.  It seems to top out at about the same rate
> quit often.
> 
> I'm wondering if I should be getting PCI controllers and wide SCSI.

When I tested that controller I was fundamentally UNipressed by the RAW I/O 
performce that it was able to attain when I had it configured to operate in 
JOBD mode.  It didn't come eve slightly close to what I could get out of 
the exact same disks on a AHA1742 controller on the same system.  I suspect 
that if you actually ask it to perform some sort of RAID functinality you 
wouldn't get any faster I/O thruput.

Your mileage may vary.

