|>Result: In all three cases the Vax counts down to 6 and then jumps to 8 
|>	again. Then it hangs.
|>	Even now there's no output on the serial Console.
|>	BTW: I'm using a Facit VT100 Compatible Terminal as the serial 
|>	Console (8N1, 19200 Baud, Serial Port on the Vax switched to 19200).
|>	Could it be that I'm using the wrong cable?
|>	Someone told me that I have to use a "special" Cable with a pinout
|>	different from standard serial connectors. Is that true?

The 9-pin connector on the BA23/BA123 boxes is *not* the same as the IBMPC 
standard. Unfortunately I cannot currently find my record of what the cable
should be but, if with the above config you still see no output on the terminal
then it seems likely that you have the wrong cable. (Mine in the lab are all
BCC08 because that is what happened to be available, but I don't have the
wiring for that either :-( )

It looks like your machine is expecting you to choose a language. I think if
you wait long enough (5-10 minutes) it times out and carries on using a
default. Not that this will help much if you can't see what is going on ...

