I went the DEC route about 6 years ago, I'll never do it again.

The reason being that back when I started my own company, I bought
a DECstation 5000. (Actually two of them)  DEC dropped that whole 
line when they went to Alpha's.  Guess how much these boxes are 
worth now?  Basically nothing.  Guess who supports API's on those
systems?  Nobody.   I now work for someone else.  So if you want to
buy a DEC ask yourself if it matters that in a week or a year you
can't get any support for what you just plunked down tens of
thousands of dollars for, and to keep up in your field you're going
to have to plunk down the same sum again for a completely different
system.
	But don't take my word on DEC's problems.  Check out the
newsgroups for DEC, SUN, and IBM.  The DEC newsgroup is always loaded
with For Sale ads for used equipment.   You won't see that in the 
other newsgroups.



