etteldor@unix-ag.uni-kl.de (Martin Etteldorf) wrote:

Meaning of hex display on rear.

F  wait for DCOK
E  wait for POK
D  checksum on cpu rom
C  searching for 64k base ram for rom console
B  read verify bus access via IPR register <q22 must be functional>
A  Testing VCB02 video console display
9  identifying console.
8  on the rear panel led indicated it want to know what language to
    use (13 possible) for console inquery.
 7  memory data tests. 
6  A stop at 6 says it's running address tests on memory.  
5  is test for q22 memory. 
4 is CPU and resgister tests. 
3 interrupt tests <would show if there is hole in the grant chain if 
   stopped here>.
2 searching for boot device with bootable file.
1 boot device found. 
0 test complete.

In the ba23 box from the first through third rows of slots quad sized
<full width> are for CPU and mem. If they are filled, starting with
the forth row they become dual width <half the full width>  bus slots.
starts with ab then CD progressing to slot 5

The bus grant progression is

ROW1  AB  Always CPU <quad width>
             v
ROW2  AB  memory quad
             v
ROW3  AB  memory quad or bus grant
             v
ROW4  AB > CD   Start of peripheral chain 
                      v
ROW5  AB < CD
             v
ROW6  AB > CD
                     v
ROW7  AB < CD
             v
ROW8  AB > CD

BA123 box is similar.

And gap in that chain must be filled with a bus grant card ror moving
boards.  Note that some cards must fall in a certain order or the
priority will cause problems.  

