Reuters Selects NCR to Expand its Data Warehouse

Provides Real-Time Information and Decision Support

Nearly $50 Million Order Includes NCR WorldMark Servers

DAYTON, Ohio, Jan. 6 /PRNewswire/ -- Reuters, a world-leading provider of
news and real-time information to more than 340,000 users, has turned to
ncr , the world leader in data warehousing, to increase the size and
capabilities of its data warehouse. 

As part of a $49.2 million contract, the computer maker will supply five
NCR WorldMark 5100M massively parallel processing (MPP) servers that will
be integrated with Reuters' existing NCR systems. 

The 5100M servers and the installed NCR 3600MPP machines -- running NCR's
Teradata relational database management system (RDBMS) and NCR TOP END
enterprise middleware software -- will form a 500-gigabyte data warehouse
valued at nearly $74 million. When completed, it will be one of the largest
commercial data warehouses in Europe. 

Information stored in the data warehouse -- which is collected from a vast
number of data sources worldwide -- is the foundation for Reuters' new 3000
Series information products for the equities, fixed income and money
markets. These products enable corporate treasurers, investment managers
and sales analysts to make more detailed analyses of markets and financial
instruments by bringing together, on a single screen, historical
information with real-time prices and news. This capability gives Reuters a
major competitive edge. 

"We are responding to a demand from the financial community for real-time
data combined with historical analysis as people increasingly use large
amounts of historical data to analyze investment opportunities," said
Jeremy Penn, Reuters' International Marketing Director for Equities.
"Upgrades will continue as we roll out the service to more of our customer
base." 

"Our needs have placed huge demands on NCR and over time it has turned into
a positive and helpful relationship. The most important requirements we had
were reliability and the ability to expand the system as the data volumes
and number of users grew," he added. 

"Our partnership with Reuters is a significant milestone for NCR. It
underscores our expertise in building large and complex data warehouses to
support global information access and decision-support systems," said Mark
Hurd, Marketing vice president for NCR's Computer Systems Group. 

The NCR WorldMark servers are to be installed in Reuters' data center in
London. A second data center is under construction in Geneva to provide
back up and load sharing. 

About NCR's WorldMark 5100M, Teradata RDBMS and TOP END Software 

NCR's large-scale data warehousing solutions consist of the WorldMark 5100M
server systems scaling to support up to 4,096 Intel processors, NCR
Teradata parallel processing relational database, and comprehensive
consulting service and support offerings that are designed to help
organizations analyze massive amounts of data to create a competitive
advantage. 

NCR's Teradata RDBMS's shared-nothing software architecture, provides
unmatched power, scalability, connectivity and case of administration
required for business-critical data warehousing applications. 

NCR's TOP END is a robust middleware that offers a scalable,
message-passing engine and distributed-application administration tools for
successfully deploying mission-critical applications across an enterprise. 

About Reuters 

Reuters Holdings PLC supplies the global business community and media with
a wide range of products, including real-time financial data, transaction
systems, access to numerical and textual historical databases, news, still
photography and news video. 

About NCR 

NCR is the leader in delivering commercial, open computer systems for
distributed application and decision-support solutions to customers in all
industries. The company also develops industry-specific platforms and
solutions for customers in the retail, financial and telecommunications
industries. 

More information on NCR can be found on the World Wide Web:
http://www.ncr.com. SOURCE NCR 




