I forget the original post.  Is this displayed on a console terminal or the LED
display on the back of the unit?

Original looks OK.  Current however, has 2 basic bus problems.  Slot 4 is a Q/CD
slot for memory.  It will work with a double height card in the upper half of
the slot, or a bus grant card in the same location.  The bus then snakes down
and up through the remaining slots, so card 2 is out of place, or move card
three below card 2 and all will be OK with the bus.

As far as the self tests, you could remove all but the CPU(12) and one memory
board, connected using the memory interconnect cable.  This should at least pass
the self tests to 3...  Test 2,1,and 0 are used during boot.  If that fails, you
could try the other memory board, eliminating the memory as the problem.
Otherwise, it would be a CPU problem.  I'm not sure, but I beleive it will also
pass self tests without and memory boards (using 1MB on CPU board), however, no
OS I know of will boot on the machine in this config.

Good Luck,

Steve
