> I have a Pentium 90 digital STARION 600i and I was wondering if I could
> just slip in a Pentium 200 CPU were the 90 CPU is and have a Pentium 200. I
> don't know if it would blow up or work fine , so somebody give me some
> advise.
> 
> Steven
> robstesc@netins.net
> 
> Please e mail the answer to me.

The 600i only supports standard Pentiums up to 133Mhz. This is based on
the clock freq. available (50Mhz, 60MHz, and 66Mhz) and the multipliers
(either 1.5x or 2x). You can put in the overdrive chips which we have
tested to 166Mhz (using the 66Mhz base freq.). The 200Mhz will not work.

