Webster Butler wrote:
> 
> Help needed, I hope this is the correct forum...
> 
> I littlte we have a New Win95 PC at work with Exceed installed on it. We
> are trying to get it to run X windows(using TCP/IP) off of our DECVMS
> nodes.
> 
> Currently our WIN95 PC is running TCPIP (Pathworks or DECNET can be
> installed if needed) and My VAX is running DECNET and FUSION 3.4 for
> TCP/IP.
> 
> When attempting a RLOGIN to hopefully start an X session our VMS nodes
> sends back a message stating the host name for my PC is unknown. I have
> entered my pc host name and ip address in the Machine.DB file in fusion and
> also on the DECwindows security menu.
> 
> Is there anything else I need to do to get this working OR is there a more
> efficient way of accomplishing my task?????
> 
> Regards,
> VMS Dummy

Webster,

You don't mention what say what IP package you are running (UCX or 
MultiNet ?).  I know that with MultiNet, I can run X-windows sessions on 
a Win95 platform with Exceed (either v4 or v5).  I don't know a lot
about
IP, but I can tell you what is involved in our set-up.  First, we use
RSH
to launch the X-window session.  The RSH call is made by Exceed to a VMS 
user account. The user account has a file ".rhosts" that lists all the 
node names allowed to use the remote services (RLOGIN and RSH) for that
account (these are the "trusted hosts" for that user).  The node names 
must be "fully qualified" and can include usernames.  For PCs, we just
list the name like

	Win95PC.d52.Lilly.com

no username required.  We use Exceed's XStart utility to launch the RSH
call, and it can also be used to run RLOGIN.

Hope this helps
-- 
