1. Start reading (if you haven't) the nice information about the new
Personal Workstation a-series at http://www.workstation.digital.com . A lot
of nice information...

2. Have a look at the SPEC-numbers at http://www.specbench.org

There you will find out that the Alpha processor outperforms the SUN
Ultra's (not to mention the Sun SPARCs), Pentium Pro's etc. Note that some
of the results are obtained with more that one processor, resulting in a
better performance.

3. If you are interested in comparing MFlops, the Pentium Pro 200MHz has a
peak performance of 200MFlops compared to the world record of 1.5GFlops
held by the Alpha (a 767MHz version with a special cooling system
http://www.kryotech.com/http/dec_1.htm ).

4. In the first test of the next Pentium Pro running at 233Mhz, code named
Klamath, at http://www.sysdoc.pair.com/klamathfirst.html you can also see
that it doesn't improve the performance that much compared to the current
Pentium Pro. It think it will take a year or so before a 300MHz Pentium Pro
is available, which is too long for you I guess.

Good Luck!

---
Anders Olsson

