A better way to get a session going on a VMS machine is to use XDM.  I'm
running Extra!X on my NT PC, connecting to an AXP machine running OpenVMS
and PathWay for Open VMS.  Both Extra!X and PathWay are products of
Attachmate Corporation...which I work for, but the two products work well
enough together that I'd want to use them even if I didn't work for the
company.  

I've got Extra!X set up to send an XDM request to a specific VMS machine
when it comes up, so I get a DECwindows login prompt, then a regular
DECwindows session.  No muss, no fuss.  This should work for any Xwindows
terminal or emulator that supports XDM connects.

