Unfortunatly for Digital, the lowly 8086, barely capable of handing a
serial port at 9600 baud has matured into something which competes
against the ALPHA.

Graphics workstation: Intel is working hard to raise the stakes. It gave
Macromedia (Makers of graphic software for the MAC) a bunch of Intel
Pentium Pro servers before they were available in exchange for
Macromedia developping its 3D product on NT instead of MAC and
