Hi,

rik_mos (Richard_Moss@bc.sympatico.ca) wrote:
: I bought a DEcpc AXP/150 ""Jenson" MoBo I want to build the computer but I 
: don't have a Manual for the Board .. any Ideas ?

Hmmm, I don't have an idea where to find a manual, but I may have some 
hints for you ...

- You can't use a standard PC power supply on the Jensen; DEC's power supply
  has 3.3V lines in addition to the standard voltages.
- You will need  an Adaptec 1742A EISA SCSI controller to connect storage
  devices. No other controller works, sorry.
- Only some VGA card work with the Jensen. I know of two EISA boards
  (ELSA Winner 1000 ISA/ISA and Compaq ProVision) that work. A simple 
  256 kB VGA board also worked for me. you can also connect a terminal to
  serial port A (9600,8N1).
- You will need parity SIMMs, either 4MB (1Mx36) or 16MB (4Mx36). The Jensen
  needs four identical SIMMs at a time. Start populating the SIMMs in the slot
  that is closest to the edge of the board and leave each second slot free
  (unless you want to insert 8 SIMMs, of course :-)).

Linux and Windows NT work fine on the Jensen, though Linux installation is a
bit hairy. For Digital Unix (OSF/1), you will need a special firmware on the 
Adaptec 1742A ("G1" firmware) that is only available from DEC. I don't know
about VMS, sorry ...

Hope this helps,
regards,
	Michael Engel	(engel@unix-ag.uni-siegen.de)
 



