|>
|>Justa nother quick question,
|>my vaxstation 3100 has the model number VS542A-BC..what model is this? I 
|>suspect it is a 38 but I'm not quite sure...
|>

The last VS3100 M38 I saw was a VS42?? not VS542. The 3100-x8 models were WS42
parts. But if the machine has been upgraded it probably still has the old box
with the old part number. If the medallion on the front says VAXstation 3100
it is probably the M30 (or M40). If it had M38 or M48 on the front you wouldn't 
be asking :-)

A VAXstation 3100 M30 calls itself a KA42A when it boots.
A VAXstation 3100 M38 calls itself a KA42B when it boots.
A VAXstation 3100 M76 calls itself a KA43-A when it boots.

The VS3100-40 is a VS3100-30 in a bigger box.
The VS3100-48 is a VS3100-38 in a bigger box.

If it doesn't boot it can be identified by the motherboard part number:

KA42A: 54-17312-01
KA42B: 54-19356-01
KA43:  54-19847-01


