This same thinking is what has many business running old hardware with old
operating systems and unsupported software.  They can not upgrade to more recent
versions of their applications, which have features they have asked for, because
their o/s will not support it.  They are having a hell of a time finding people
to convert their current data to something current and it is costing them a
fortune for new hardware, operating system, applications, and retraining on the
new applications.  Lots of them are still putting it off, thinking that someone
will drop the solution into their laps..

Most of these problems and costs could have been reduced or eliminated with a
reasonable schedule for upgrade/replacement.  With this method, current hardware
still has market value for trade ups, rather than starting from scratch and
replacing everything. 

01-JAN-00  is coming awfully quick for some of these people.

