To cast out the demons of Microsoft:

	1. Preach the Gospel of the One True Operating system.
	Whether that is SysV, BSD, Linux, Plan 9, etc...  
	All sit at the Right Hand of UNIX.

	2. Become missionaries unto the unenlightened.  Do not 
	condemn or berate them--teach them.

	3. Choose your battles wisely.  

	4. Tithe.  Write good, interesting and useful code and
	copyleft it.
	
	5. Be honest.  






Sermon notes:

	*1. Insert your favorite portable, pre-emptive multi-taksing,
	multi-user, network-aware, POSIX compliant, open-standard
	look-alike, robust Operating System here.

	*2. Eventually, they'll go bankrupt or get promoted to 
	management (The Dilbert Principle).  If you berate them,
	you only look pushy and defensive.  Tell them what they're
	missing.

	*3. Fight to keep the back-end servers UNIX, but don't bother
	with the secretary's PC.  You'll lose.  She'll bring one from
	home if you do win.

	*4. Overwhelm the competition with something that actually
	works--and cheap.  'Nuff said.

	*5. UNIX has no well-documented, easy-to-use, state-of-the-art
	universally-accepted Office Automation tools.  Just admit 
	defeat here ('till #4 gets going more).  You want a good Web 
	Server, Firewall, File Server, etc...  UNIX wins.

