Me (edwardsw@cadvision.com) wrote:

: Hello Digital Gurus!

: I have two Digital Vax 4000 servers running OpenVMS 6.1. Also, on my network I 
: have a DEC Server 200 Terminal Server. Now today, when I powered the DecServer 
: 200 up (for the first time in over 3 years) I cannot do anything with it. My 
: terminal server just stays black and the wait light is always on. On the 
: server, the first 3 green LED's are always on and the fourth just blinks at 
: me. I fully expected to see a local prompt or something to tell me what the 
: hell this box is doing. But alas, it's documentation disappeared years ago. I 
: do remember that it worked years ago and then I quit using it, now we have 
: hired another administrator and they need to have 2 terminals connected to the 
: vax at all times. If my memory is correct, when I plug in the terminals I 
: should see a LOCAL> prompt. Is this a configuration problem? Is it dead? 
: (Highly unlikley) Do I need to reboot the servers so it knows that this thing 
: exists? Do I need to configure it through the network using NCP? LATCP? How do 
: I configure it? Help! Please! Please reply by e-mail to 
: edwardsw@cadvision.com. Thank you very much.

: - Will

The DS200 loads its software via the MOP_MOM DownLine Load protocol from
a supporting load host (VMS or Ultrix).  Make sure your VAX is running
the MOP_MOM listener and has the correct DS200 load module available
in the usual directory.  

If you hook up a 9600 baud terminal to Port 1, you can watch it power up
and send out a DownLine Load Request.  If no load host responds within
a timeout, it will keep trying every few minutes.  If you got that far,
the DS200 is OK and you just need to configure some VAX to answer.

Barry Kort



