I have run lattice QCD codes on a 200Mhz Pentium Pro (Linux + Absoft f77) and
a 250Mhz AlphaStation (DEC Unix + DEC f77). My benchmarks were 40+Mflops for
the Pentium Pro, and 70+Mflops for the AlphaStation. I have also developed
lattice QCD codes (not precisely the same ones, but similar) for the CRAY T3D,
in CFT77. These only ran at about 20Mflops/node. As I understand it, the 
problem here is that the T3D has no L3 cache, whereas the AlphaStations and
(most of) the Alpha based clones do.
