In article <32e17860.448352@news2.ibm.net>, abaddon@ibm.net (Michael Ross) writes:

:...  Already running NT on an AXP 150. The
:console on the 3000-800 is very different  - no ARC, no menu-driven
:console, no OS_TYPE env. to set - just a basic VAX/DEC5000 type
:console. So...
:
:1. is there any way of persuading NT to run on these things? How?

   Sure... Feel like writing some NT device drivers?  :-)

   A quick check of the Microsoft NT pages (best course of action
   when considering running NT on any particular collection of Intel
   or Alpha hardware) will show this system is not listed among the
   supported hardware platforms -- and with good reason, as NT does
   not include any drivers for any turbochannel widgets needed/used
   by the DEC 3000 series.

   NT is supported on the DECpc AXP 150 (aka DEC 2000), most (all?)
   members of the AlphaStation and AlphaServer series, on some of
   Alpha boards, and on the Multia series.  It is not supported on
   the DEC 3xxx, DEC 4xxx, DEC 7xxx or similar series Alpha boxes.

