>you are hardware(illy) technically correct - BUT - verryy confusing also.
>
>There was in fact one (optionally 2) physical PPU units - AND -
>in fact each ran at 100 ns/instruction - BUT -
>software(illy) each ran 10 process streams as physical memory was about 1
>us.
>There were 10 P Registers, 10 ...   - AND -
>appeared to software people as 10 separate independent processors.
>
>Which is very confusing at first glance.
