Scripts for Cluster 1.0 SP1 work fine.  (Be on the look out for Cluster 1.1
in March with IP Failover, Dual SQL, Lotus Notes Failover!)  Scripts can do
everything that the NT Command Prompt can do, i.e. net start, net send,
start, etc.
You should put the script on each cluster node in identical directories. 
If you put it on the shared storage you may have a time problem on the
Start script.  If you have a program that you want to start you may want to
use Srvany to make it a service, then use a CMD file with a Net start of
that service.  The stop scripts should return control back to the cluster
manager quickly.  This can be done with Call,Start statement from the core
CMD.
