>(Oh Jaehoon) writes:
>
>Is there anyone who knows the floating-point representation
>in Digital Alpha Station, DEC OS.
>
>I would like to exchange float numbers between IBM PC, Alpha Station,
>and Sun Sparc Station via TCP protocol.

The AlphaStation and the IBM PC use the same format, little-endian IEEE
floating.  The Sun uses big-endian IEEE float, which means you'll have to
swap the bytes when transferring between the Sun and either of the other
two systems.

