Robin Birch  <robin.birch@royalmail.co.uk> wrote:
>Dear All,
>Well I've got it all going, thanks for all the help that people have
>given me.  Unfortunately I've had a minor disaster.  Whilst setting
>everything up there was a lack of DC lights and a nice smell of hot
>electrics.
>
>Well I switched it all off, worked out what I had done wrong and tried
>again.  The system worked fine except the run lights on the two BA23s
>won't come on.  I guess I've melted something.
>
>Can some one fax me the schematics for the circuity behind the run light
>circuits so that I can go look.  The system works fine so I guess its
>something on the display side of the system.

It may not be related to your display problem (or it may be related,
it's hard to tell!), but the "smell of hot electrics" in a BA23 is
almost inevitably related to charred power cables between the
power supply and backplane, or between the power supply and disk
drives.  Look "behind" the run light panel and check out the power
supply harnesses.  In particular, check for deformed metal contacts
or charred connector housings on the 18-pin harness.  When you
find these, replace the harness with a quality one.  I build mine
using gold-plated connectors and 14-gauge wire.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



