I had some free time so we ran some benchmarks of my
code across several platforms that I have access to.

The code is for Monte Carlo simulations of dipolar
fluids in the grand canonical ensemble.  It involves
lots of floating point calculations with complex variables
and has very little I/O.

Nearly all calculations are done using double precision
arithmetic.  The same source code was use on all platforms
(ie. no hand tuning was done for any of the architectures).

For 5 million MC steps, these are the results:

                                        Time    Rel. Speed  
             Type                      (CPUs)  (to DEC 3000/500)
==========================================================
sp2 4 nodes  Parallel (5M steps/node)  3480.0     0.98
	     (total of 20M MC steps)
