This is similar to what we see.  We have a 300MHz 21164 Alpha (2M L3
cache) and a dual PPro 200 (256K L2 cache).  We ran some FFT code on
both.  Both run Windows NT 4.0.  The code was compiled on the Alpha
using MSVC++ 4.0, the PPro was MSVC++ 4.2.  The Alpha executable was
optimized for speed and the 21164.  The PPro executable was optimized
for speed and the Pentium.  The FFT code runs on only one CPU.  The
Alpha was 33% faster than the PPro on the closest tests.  It was about
100% faster on some tests.  The FFT code was instrumented so we could
get some other results so it wasn't as much of a floating point
instruction stream as it could have been.



