The drive is older than it looks.  It's from early 1992; it won a MacUser
award that year.  At the time, one gigabyte was a lot of storage.

The three pairs of jumpers closest to the outside edge set the SCSI ID.
The seventh pair from the outside, if set, is to spin up on power-up.

There's a pair of jumpers just behind the round holes for the
termination resistor packs.  If the resistors are installed, set both 
pairs of jumpers.

