> In particular, DEC compilers can only help when they are used.
> The FX!32 support for running Intel binaries on Alpha does not
> have access to program source so cannot benefit from compiler
> technology.

Why can't FX!32 benefit from compiler technology?  Source code is
pretty much irrelevant for the optimizer in FX!32.  We use many compiler
techniques in the FX!32 optimizer in addition to many techniques which
standard compilers cannot use (because of the available profile and
alignment
data).  X86 instructions are our source code.

We pushed for byte/word instructions in Alpha to: 

1) speed up x86 program execution (having byte/word instructions is
   *always* better thean not having them in the x86 code case).

2) aid in the porting of device drivers.

3) and probably many other reasons that I don't recall.

...tom



