Christopher Cannon wrote:
> 
> Can anyone tell me why my Starion 930 will not support a True Color 24
> bit display mode when the manual (as inadequate as it is) vaguely states
> that it will?  My Windows 95 doesn't even show True Color as an option,
> but I know it exists.  Do I need to replace my video card or get a new
> driver?  Any info is greatly appreciated.
> 
>                                         Chris Cannon

The 930 will support 24-bit color at 640x480 with the latest S3 video
drivers. You can find the drivers at:

http://www.pc.digital.com/~ftp/index/ix_VIDEO.htm

the current driver is:

VS002119.EXE - S3 Trio 732/764/765 Windows 95 Driver v2.11.03 [173K
07/24/96]

The way to figure out if your video card supports a particular
resolution and color depth is to multiply the horizontal resolution by
the vertical resolution by the number of bits of color divided by 8.

ex. at 800x600 at 24-bits color ("true color")

800 x 600 = 480,000 x 24 = 11,520,000 / 8 = 1,440,000 (1.44MB)

So, as you can see, for 800x600 at 24-bits you would need 1.44MB of
video memory (your system comes with 1MB video memory).

regards,

glen kelley



