Considering defunct machines with easily understandable command languages,
one must however give much credit to Dr. Ann Wang for the Wang VS series
machines.  The entire operating system was based on IBM 370 instructions,
however every single function was available to users administrators and
operators through the use of menu options.  It was possible to work on this
machine for years without ever entering a single command.

Moreover, the file/library management features resembled that of Windows
File Manager, and it was also possible to write very straight forward
scripts to run almost any job.  Just about any program written for this
machine was entirely parameter driven, and every parameter could be
ascertained by simply running the program by hand, filling out the screen,
and making some notes as to screen name and field name on the way.

It was really too bad to see this machine disappear, as has most of Wang
Labs today.  Those who used it left the environment kicking and
screaming...  They were so easy to use, that most people felt incompetent
to move on to the more traditional command oriented machines.  Even long
time IS people.

