> Was not MIX the publishing language created by Knuth?  Or do I have it confused
> with something else?  Bob

Close.  MIX was the example programming language Knuth used in his The
art of Computer Programming, basically a simple minded assembly language
for a non-existent machine (but one which had a lot of programs written
for it in various computer science courses).

Named for Tom Mix, of cowboy fame.

