The 7 track drives at the Univac at UMCP were tuned to play
Christmas carols by writing various block sizes to them.
I knew something was up as a friend of mine on staff there
was shown on the status monitor as running a batch job
(which he never did), but that was evidentally the only
way to run the program.

The Univac was really a musical thing.  Later on, the same
friend was a little hard up for something to do on New Year's
Eve so he went in to watch the computer consoles tick over
to the new year (IBM VM beeps and prints the date/time every
day at midnight).  Well to his surprise, just after the
consoles beeped, the SMU on the UNIVAC started to play
Old Lang Syne.  It's an annual thing, but nobody there
had ever heard it because the facility is usually closed
on New Years Eve.  They rolled the clock back and sure
enough it did play it.

Several years later many of us were at a party at my house
and were trying to figure out what we should do at the
moment of midnight.  Then we got the idea, and sure enough
a long distance call to the U of M machine room got them
to hold the phone up to the Univac so we could hear it
play...



