> Recently I don't succeed anymore to run DCL commands on a specific
> remote thru SYSMAN:
> That is what I type and receive:
> $ MC SYSMAN SET ENB�VIRONMEMT/NODE=XYZ/USER=ABC
> Remote Password:
> .....
> SYSMAN> DO SHOW USERS ! or any other command
> %SYSMAN-I-OUTPUT, command execution on node XYZ
> %SYSMAN-I-NODERR,error returned from node XYZ
> -SMI-E-BADACTRL, remote access control info invalid
> 
> Remarks:
> 2) It works well with another username on the same remote node
> 
> Thank you for any suggestion

That's the old annoying problem: you changed your password on the 
remote node XYZ at some stage, but the SMISERVER process there still
remembers the old password.

Login to XYZ, do a STOP/IDEN=<SMISERVER-pid> there.
Restart SMISERVER on XYZ with
   $ @SYS$SYSTEM:STARTUP SMISERVER

Good luck!
	Thomas Schmid



