I'm coming into this late, but some other nits follow.

Make that:

SD0021  EXEC PGM=IEFBR14

(Unless you've made IEFBR14 a JCL procedure which invokes PGM=IEFBR14.)

There was a rumor that IEFBR14 (IEF meaning it was one of a group of
utility programs provided by IBM, BR14 standing for Branch Register 14,
a machine instruction that, in this instance, results in returning to
the caller, which, in this instance, is the operating system with all
the file processing in the step's DD statements done) failed to perform
its other stated purpose, to set register 15, the system return code, to
0.  Even what ended up as a two machine instruction program was
incorrect when initially released.

-Fred



