>Oh, changing directories and volumes was a real pain in the ass.  Even more,
> way too much
>typing.  Luckily, I had a script that reduced it all to a simple "cd" command

As has been remarked elswhere on this thread.  VMS's command language leaves a 
lot to be desired.  It was designed with a lot of good intentions: 
sort-of-English-like syntax, orthogonality, comprehensible command names.  
However, the product doesn't match the dream.  On the other hand, I do find it 
a lot easier to remember commands than in Unix, which I learned several years 
before VMS came to market.  Now for a command language that came closer to 
realizing its designers intentions, I would recommend Data General's AOS, 
AOS/VS CLI.  Like a lot of good technology,. you may consider it defunct.


