> Small quibble, was not the machine just called the 6600.  The "Cyber" thing came
> a bit later.  I am not sure of this, but if there is some old Control Data types
> out there, I am sure we will get the right answer.

It was the CDC 6600. Cybers came in about 70/71 as replacements
for the 6K machines. You still needed the rubber mallet and a plumber
thought ;)

Not anOperating System was MUCH later. SCOPE was the thing on 6K and earlier
( 60 bit ) Cybers.

After a PDP-6, the rate a Cyber-72 ran jobs was frightenly fast. TIME to
get them was about 5 times slower... IE what took 10 min on the 6, took
a second or two on the cyber. But you could not see it for another 3 or
4 hours in the print queue :(

~Paul
still have a SCOPE internals manual some where I think...



