In comp.sys.dec Terry C. Shannon <shannon@world.std.com> wrote:
> According to collateral released by Digital, the additional cost for 2MB 
> of L3 cache is $950. But, due to the fact that the Miata systems use the 
> new Pyxis core logic chip (as opposed to the predecessor 21071/21172 core 
> logic chipsets), an uncached 433a system performs better than a 433 system 
> with 2MB of L3 cache.

Thats consistent with what I've heard.  Numbers I've seen so far:
Estimates for the PWS 433a SPECint95 is 12+ and SPECfp95 is 15+.
Estimates for the PWS 500a SPECint95 is 14  and SPECfp95 is 18 .


(from Burkhard Neidecker-Lutz):
                        SPECint95       SPECfp95
PC164/1MB L3            14.6            13.9            (aka Enorex Ultra 500s)
PC164/2MB L3            14.9            16.0
AlphaStation 500/500    15.0            20.4                             

Getting better performance on a 433 Mhz L3'less machine then the current
500 Mhz 1 mb L3 machines is impressive.

I believe (but not sure) the 433a numbers mentioned above are without L3,
and 500a numbers are with 2 mb cache.  Clarifications welcome.

