Thomas Leitner (tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at) wrote:
[...]
: Now I see a strange behaviour which I have never seen on any other
: machine, PC or workstation: The external SCSI disks (a ST32550N and
: a CFP4207) do *not* spin up when the machine is not powered up.
[...]
: Questions:
:
: 1.) Can anyone explain this to me. What does it depend upon ?
:     TERM Power perhaps?

I think so. Several disk drives (from various manufacturers) don't
spin up when signal levels on the SCSI bus are improper.
(I suspect the RST (SCSI reset) line.)

Try to set one of the drives to "supply TERMPWR to SCSI bus" or
whatever it's called and the problem should go away.
(If termination in the workstation is provided by an internal disk
you might have to set it to "TERMPWR from drive or SCSI bus" or
alike.)

: 2.) Can the disks be damaged or something. 

AFAIK: no. (YMMV!)


--
Ralf.




