>Several questions:
>1) How does this machine compare in performance to current Alphas?

Slower.  Current Alpha systems are running a generation and half
more modern Alpha implementation at clock speeds in the range of
300+ Mhz.  The built-in SCSI adapters of the Model 600 support
Fast SCSI, which is comparible to any built-in Fast/Narrow SCSI
adapters on recent systems.  However, many recent systems are
using Fast/Wide SCSI.

>To the current crop of Pentium Pro server boxes?

Also probably slower, since the Pentium Pro systems probably
have a faster clock as well.  A modern server might also have
a better I/O subsystem.

