:run my compiler (Visual C++ or Borland C++) and Office on a DEC Multia
:running NT 3.5 or NT 4.0?

   FX!32 is a translator/interpreter, and is useful for many applications.
   In the specific case of translating/interpreting a compiler or an
   assembler via a tool like FX!32, it may (will?) produce a compiler
   that runs on the new platform, but the compiler will still generate
   binary code for the old platform.

   Various Microsoft products include support NT on Alpha in much the
   same fashion as the NT distribution CD-ROM kits.  Recent versions of
   the Microsoft Visual C++ package do include support for generating
   binaries for use on Windows NT on Alpha.  I don't have information
   on a version of Microsoft Office for Windows NT on Alpha -- check
   with Microsoft, or check the glyphs present on the side of the
   Microsoft software distribution box.  Or the manual.  (Those I've
   always believed that `Reading the manual is admitting defeat'.  :-)

