k.d. wrote:
> 
> I have read about FX/32 for Alphas. Can I use this product to
> run my compiler (Visual C++ or Borland C++) and Office on a DEC Multia
> running NT 3.5 or NT 4.0?

Development environments are specifically not supported under FX!32.
From the readme for v1.0:

      o  x86 compiler IDE's (Interactive Development Environments)
         are not supported under this version of Digital FX!32.

         In general, compiler IDE's (such as those for various C,
         C++, and Fortran compilers) are hard-coded for a
         particular architecture and access the system in ways
         that are not supported by Digital FX!32.  Therefore, x86
         compiler IDE's are restricted under this version of
         Digital FX!32.  This restriction does not apply to
         interpreters, such as Microsoft Visual Basic.

On the other hand, it might be possible to just run the compiler, if
producing x86 code on an Alpha is what you really want to do.

Office95 is supported under FX!32 v1.0, and it works fine: I've been
running it for quite a while.

Office97 is currently unsupported, but I installed it the other day
anyway (using a different version of FX!32): the parts I care about seem
to work for me.

FX!32 is only supported on Windows NT 4.0, but there are instructions in
the readme for running it on 3.51 at you own risk.
