Ever since we had a 5 hour power outtage on our RAID 410s, they've been
behaving strangely. Once or twice a day, the RAID sets will become
unavailable and require a controller reset and filesystem remount.

We believe it is something to do with the backup batteries ... the
diagnostics indicate they are low and the manual says that if they drop
below a certain level then the RAID sets will automatically drop
off-line. 

The systems have been behaving for a year but have never had power off
for longer than an hour before. 

Currently both are OK but one indicates low charge ... the RAID sets are
still OK.

DEC pointed us to a firmware fix wish addressed erroneous battery charge
warnings, but this hasn't stopped the problem.

Has anyone else seen this happen ?

