In article <32d6c76c.23631695@news.teleport.com>,
Carl Snyder <lemac@teleport.com> wrote:
>The 40 pin Berg connector on the DL11, Berg P/N 65424-008, DEC P/N 12-09941-02
>was manufactured by Berg Electronics.  According to Berg, the matching female
>connector for the attaching cable was manufactured by a different DEC
>sub-contractor, unknown to Berg.  Where can I buy the connector to make new
>cables?

If you're going for discrete wire termination, there are several choices
available.  Digi Key (1-800-DIGI-KEY) sells AMP and Waldom connectors
of this style.  You could get a 40 pin AMP housing as part number
A3044-ND, and then buy the contacts A3000-ND for as many circuits
as you need.

IDC connectors (for ribbon cable) are readily available from a number
of sources.  If you only are going to be using, say, 5 circuits, and
these are going to a DB-25 connector, say, it's entirely possible
to take a 5-conductor ribbon cable and route each wire to the pins
you want on 40-pin and DB-25 IDC connectors.  The result 
isn't as professional looking or sturdy as
going the discrete termination route, but it does work.  I believe
Doug Jones posted some very good details about the procedure some
time back (whether for 20mA or RS-232, I can't remember.)  I'm cross-
posting to alt.sys.pdp8 in the hope he or someone else there still
has the original article.

>  Also, does anyone have a source for 8 pin, 20 mA current loop male
>connectors?

Ooh, I think DEC still sells them, but I don't have the part number.
Digi-Key sells 8-position in-line AMP Mate-N-Loks, but I can't guarantee
these are the same as the ones DEC uses, since there appear to be multiple
series of Mate-N-Lok connectors out there.  The Digi-Key part numbers
are A14275-ND for a plug housing, A14272-ND for a cap housing, and
the corresponding parts for the contacts are A1436-ND for the pin
and A1437-ND for the housing.  If someone can verify that these indeed
are the same series as the connectors DEC uses, I would be very interested.
I've been cannibalizing old cables for the connectors as I need them.

I'm not affiliated with Digi-Key; just very, very happy with their
service and selection.  They even offer a Canadian $ catalog now!

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



