Ivan,

It's a Phoenix BIOS, right?  Boot the system to the DOS prompt, try
Ctrl-Alt-Esc and Ctrl-Alt-S, two chords often used by a Phoenix BIOS.
If this doesn't work, there may be a jumper on the motherboard set to
inhibit you from getting into the CMOS setup.  Also, look on the
motherboard for a jumper to invalidate the CMOS setup.  No, that's not
a good idea, unless you have a record of your CMOS settings
somewhere... Ben Myers 

