In <5abg9u$sr7@usenet.rpi.edu> songi@rpi.edu wrote;

>> I am wondering (since have have hardly no money for a complete upgrade, ie
>> motherboard + chip) how I can upgrade the video card on the DECpc MTE.
>> This particular system has a VESA dedicated video card slot.  However,
>> this particular motherboard has a video output connector integrated
>> directly into the motherboard.  In the manual, I can not find anything
>> about how you can upgrade the video card (disabling the video output 
>> connector on the motherboard). My system has only 1 meg ram video
>> memory (which is a hassle).  Any suggestions are appreciated.  Thank you
>> for your time.

I have just upgraded my MTE. This is my second
upgrade from the original one. (33MHz => Dx4-100MHz ==> Pentium 133MHz)

My recommendation is to abondon EISA MB and change to PCI one.
In this case you have to enlarge the Video card slot of your
case with a nibbler. But it is relatively an easy job.
You may have to also modify the box to accept serial and
parallel ports as well.

The investment is relatively small and you can rely on the
very good power supply and cooling fan and the box itself.

1) PCI Motherboard like ASUS about $150
2) Pentium CPU about $200
3) memory at least 32MB about $150

All other ISA cards like ISDN, Adaptec, SB etc. are
reusable.

enjoy!

