That pesky '#' sign means the terminal server is password protected. You
may have to get some manuals and physical access to that box. Hopefully,
there may be a jumper or a command that can be issued from a direct
plugged in console that will flush it's memory along with the password
that it is asking for. AFter that, you should get a terminal server
prompt. 

