>Is there anyway to easily detirmine if it is the cdrom itself?  

Locate someone else with the same model CD drive working in their
system, and hook yours up in its' place for a test. It should be
a fairly generic EIDE drive, so most drivers should be able to 
at least read a disc.

If you've been playing with configurations, make sure the drive
is jumpered properly, and is connected to the correct interface.

It could be your interface cable; borrow or buy a spare IDE cable
and try swapping it out. It'd probably cost less than shipping 
the drive back.


