In article <5atktt$35l$1@jake.esu.edu>, jking@phoenix.lhup.edu says...
>
>I need the steps on a vax to forward mail using smtp to a digital unix machine.
>I believe on the vax we are using something called VAX-Mail or something like
>that.
>
>We tried to do a set forward with SMTP%"userid@address" with no luck.
>
>Any suggestions would be welcome.
>
>Joseph C King
>Unix Admin
>jking@phoenix.lhup.edu

  You need to be running some type of TCP/IP product on the system to send
SMTP mail.  Part of the TCP/IP package should have provided a shareable image
to support SMTP.  The file should be in the SYS$SHARE directory and should have
a filename of the form *_MAILSHR.EXE where '*' is the foreign mail transport
name.  Different vendors used different names for their SMTP port.  If 
SMTP_MAILSHR.EXE isn't there, there might be an IN_MAILSHR.EXE.  You would 
use the IN_MAILSHR.EXE transport by addressing the mail to IN%"user@node".

  bill.thomson@srs.gov




