This really is a FAQ......but anyhow:

a single " is parsed away and only causes the content of "..." to be passed 
literrally, ie no change to upper case or interpretation of the @ as a 
special character, denominating a file to be read.

What then is actually stored as forwarding address is 

SMTP%userid@address

as SHOW FORWARD will tell you.

As in DCL, you have to include double-" inside the quoted string to give you
a single " in the parsed result, ie

SET FORWARD SMTP%"""userid@address""" will result in 
            SMTP%"userid@address"

according to the rules above, as again SHOW FORWARD will tell you ....


Cheers 

Uwe



