Austin J. Gibbons, M.D. wrote:
> Snip....

>      The question is how do we get the Thrustmaster to work, without
> having to reset the BIOS after evry reboot?
> 
> Thanks for your help.
> 
> Austin

The sound card should be configured with the P&P jumper set to disabled.

Load the drivers from the diskette (prior to this remove all devices
from
device manager - joystick, ESS, etc.. make sure that ALL devices that
have
to do with the sound card are removed).

To enable the joystick follow the directions below (these are in the
README.TXT
contained on the diskette - the /J:e is what turns on the joystick).
Reboot and
see if the joystick is there, if not you may have to install the
joystick from 
within Win95 (via Add New Hardware).

----------------------------------------
Copy the file ESSCFG.EXE from the diskette to C:\WINDOWS\SYSTEM

* Enable the proper IRQ's by adding the following lines to the beginning
of
  AUTOEXEC.BAT (edit the AUTOEXEC.BAT found in C:\)

      set BLASTER=A220 I5 D1 T4
      C:\windows\system\ESSCFG.EXE /A:220 /I:5 /D:1 /M:s /B:330 /J:e

This line is equivalent to selecting I/O Address 220, IRQ 5, and DMA 1
for the card; selecting I/O Address 330 and sharing the IRQ for the
MPU401
section; and enabling the joystick port within the ESSCFG utility.

regards,

glen kelley



