Eric Turner wrote:
> 
> I'm in need of some help:
> 
> I have a Starion 915 system (limited to 1MB Video RAM).  I've purchased
> a new Diamond Stealth 3D 4mb card and installed it.  Seems to work fine,
> but Win95 still sees the onboard S3 Trio 32 "card" in the system.  There
> is NO REFERENCE that I can find in my tech manual to disable the onboard
> video.  Does anyone know how to disable it before I get a hammer??!!!
> 
> Thanks!  Eric     eturner@ccia.com

Win95 see the S3 chip but if you check the properties in the device
manager you will see that it is disabled. Do not remove from Device
Manager as it will attempt to re-install the next time you boot. This is
not a problem, it is disabled in BIOS when you plug in the new video
card (thats how it knows to send the video out the proper connctor).

regards,

glen kelley



