...

Before answering that question, let me first answer the related
question, "Why don't people buy more Alphas?"  Four clues to give the
answer:

Clue 1: From the earlier post by DEC employee "Randy":
    
 "I can't really go into the reasons on an open forum like this but
  suffice to say that DEC made a conscious decision not to market to
  the home sales segment. We are targeting the business market (as always)."

Clue 2: Unlike 10 years ago, the realities of this world are that
  most people who use real office computers by day can afford and in fact
  have home computers. 

Clue 3: People are extra cost conscious when buying home systems
  (obviously with their own money).  

Clue 4: Only super performance freaks would want to have to learn how
  to use two totally different computer systems instead of just one.

