What A coincidence!

I have just upgraded my video card on my DECpc MTE to a VL-BUS STB
Pegasus controller. I just removed the video card included, and
installed the STB in the other VL-BUS slot. You just connect the video
to the video card's VGA connector. I haven't tried the onboard one to
see if it works though.

In Windows 95 it is a good idea to remove the old video card drivers
before allowing Windows 95 to detect, and install the new one. If you
don't do that, then 95 thinks that the new driver conflicts with the old
one, and doesn't give it any resources.


