> PCI cards and "DEC" EISA and/of PCI cards?
> 

There are two major differences between EISA and PCI and that is the bus
speed.  EISA is capable of transferring 32MB per second and PCI 133 MB/s. 
EISA requires the configuration files (on diskette) and PCI doesn't.    PCI
cards (these days) cost alot less than their EISA cousins.  


>    We want to add more functianality to our Alpha 2100.  It should be 
> less costly to procure non DEC cards if they will work.
> 

Be careful what to buy!  If you are running OpenVMS check your SPD and
release notes before you leap.  Few third party devices are supported out
of the box.  Besides the DIGITAL brand PCI options are very competitive in
price/performance/compatibility.  Also check the "used" market if you have
DEC maintenance.

