It is more traditional to put the CPU in slot 1, and the memory in
the next slot.

Keep in mind the rules regarding CD slots in a BA23.  In a regular
"single" BA23 box the first three slots don't have any Q-bus
signals in the CD side.  I don't know how things work in a "twin"
box.

Your system still sounds rather small, but check out the power
supply harnesses, especially if you're putting a KDA50 in.  Discolored
insulation on the wires or connectors indicates that they should
immediately be replaced.  Once one of the 5V conductors opens up,
the rest have to carry the load it was carrying.  Then they heat
up even more, and open up too.  "Smoke Signals" usually begin
coming out when there are only two or three good conductors left.

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



