:	The 21164PC is a 1Q97 volume CPU.  When can we expect Exponential?
:	How will a $1000 Exponential part compete on the low-end with
:	a $400 dollar 21164PC part?  It won't.  The 21164PC will be in
:	under $3000 PC's by 1Q97.  Can't say the same for the Exponential
:	part.

	This is all well and good. DEC Alpha has been the performance leader 
for quite a while. But DEC keeps bleeding.
	So what will *compel* the consumer actually buy the Alpha ? 
Exponential and Merced have Mac and Wintel with millions of installed base
and lots of software floating around.
	Meanwhile NT RISC is dying big time, dropping off MIPS and PPC. Yes 
Alpha has a chance here being the last and best surviving NT RISC platform. 
But that is quite a gamble with not much alternative. DEC is crazy to bet the 
farm on Alpha NT. Going to bed with MS is going to one's deathbed.
	DEC has been on top in performance for a long time, but things have 
not gone too well. What is going change ? An upturn in NT sales ? Perhaps, but 
I think DEC should be a bit smarter and hedge its bets a lot better than it 
has in the past. NT is currently nearly Intel-only. It is not obvious at all 
that people will move from Intel (P6/P7) to Alpha for a bit of added speed.
They certainly haven't yet, by and large.
	And if Apple/Next takes off, as I hope it will, even NT Intel will 
have its own increased battle to fight, never mind NT RISC.

